hadiths[68]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1601","Miqdad (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that he asked: O Messenger of Allah! What do you think if I encounter a disbeliever, and he fights me, then he strikes my hand with a sword and cuts it off, then he flees from me and takes refuge by a tree and says: ""I have believed in Allah,"" so O Messenger of Allah! Should I kill him even after his declaration? The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Do not kill him."" I said: O Messenger of Allah! He has cut off my hand, and he said this after cutting off my hand, so should I kill him? The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Do not kill him. The position you had before killing him is now his, and (if you kill him) your position will be what his was before he declared the testimony."""
"1602","It is narrated from Ubaidullah bin Adi bin Khiyar that a man whispered to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; we did not know what he whispered to you ﷺ, until the Messenger of Allah ﷺ spoke loudly, and it became clear that he was seeking advice about killing a man from among the hypocrites. So the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Does he not bear witness that there is no deity except Allah?"" The man said: Yes, but his testimony will not benefit him. You ﷺ said: ""Does he not perform prayer?"" The man said: Yes, but his prayer is of no use to him. The Prophet ﷺ said: ""These are the people whom Allah has forbidden me to kill."""
"1603","It is narrated from Usama bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: ""I was present in three hypocritical gatherings of Abdullah bin Ubayy."""
"1604","It is narrated from Thabit bin Dhahak (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever commits suicide with anything in this world, will be punished with that very thing on the Day of Resurrection."""
"1605","It is narrated from Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is not permissible to kill a Muslim except for one of three reasons: becoming a disbeliever after having faith (apostasy), committing adultery while being married, or killing someone unjustly."""
"1606","It is narrated from Uthman bin Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The blood of a Muslim man is lawful in only one of three cases: apostasy after faith, adultery after marriage, or unjustly killing a soul."""
"1607","It is narrated from Zaid bin Aslam (may Allah have mercy on him) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Whoever changes his religion (Islam), kill him."""
"1608","Abdur Rahman bin Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul Qari narrates that a man came to Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) from Abu Musa (Ash'ari) (may Allah be pleased with him). Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) asked him about the condition of the people there, and he informed him. Then he asked: ""Is there any news concerning distant regions?"" The man said: ""Yes, a man became apostate after accepting Islam."" Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) asked: ""What did you do with him?"" He said: ""We seized him and struck his neck."" Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""Why did you not imprison him for three days, and give him a loaf of bread each day, and urge him to repent? Perhaps he would have repented and accepted Allah's command."" Then Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""O Allah! I was neither present there, nor am I pleased with this news, nor did I command it when it came to my knowledge."""
"1609","It is narrated from Sa'id bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Whoever is killed while protecting his wealth is a martyr."""
"1610","It is narrated from Sa'id bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""And whoever is killed while protecting his wealth is a martyr."""
"1611","It is narrated from Sa'id bin al-Musayyib (may Allah have mercy on him) that 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) killed five or seven men in retaliation for one man whom they had killed deceitfully, and 'Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""If all the people of Sana'a (a famous city in Yemen) had participated in this murder, I would have killed them all in retaliation."""
"1612","It is narrated from Amr bin Dinar (may Allah have mercy on him) that he heard from Bijalah, who said: Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) wrote (to his governors): ""Kill every male and female magician."" Bijalah said: Then we killed three magicians."
"1613","It is narrated and we have been informed that Umm al-Mu'mineen Sayyidah Hafsah (may Allah be pleased with her) killed one of her slave girls who had practiced magic on her."
"1614","Narrated from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""O Aisha! Do you know that regarding the matter about which I sought guidance, Allah has given me guidance about it."" For a considerable period, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) was in such a state that he would think he had intercourse with one of his wives, although he had not. Two men (angels) came to me, one stood at my feet and the other at my head. The one standing at my feet said to the one at my head: ""What is the matter with this man?"" The other replied: ""He has been bewitched."" He asked: ""Who has bewitched him?"" He replied: ""Labeed bin A'sam (the Jew)."" He then asked: ""With what has he bewitched him?"" He said: ""With a comb and the hair that falls from the head with the comb, inside the husk of a date-palm, which is placed in the well of Dharwan."" The narrator said: Then the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) brought it out and said: ""This is what was shown to me in my dream, as if its date-palm trees were like the heads of devils, and its water was like the infusion of henna."" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ordered it to be removed, and it was removed. Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: I said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Why not (i.e., why did you not make the counter-magic public)?"" He (ﷺ) said: ""Now Allah has cured me, and I dislike to spread evil among the people because of it."" He said: Labeed bin A'sam was a man from Banu Zuraiq, who were allies of the Jews."
"1615","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-As (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Whoever kills a sparrow or anything smaller than that without a just cause, Allah will question him about its killing."" It was asked: ""O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)! What is its right?"" He (ﷺ) said: ""That he should slaughter it and then eat it, and not cut off its head and then use it for target practice."""
"1616","Ikrimah (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated that when Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) received the news that Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) had burned apostates and irreligious people, he said: ""If I had been in his place, I would not have burned them; rather, I would have killed them, because the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Whoever changes his religion (Islam), kill him.' And I would not have burned them because the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'It is not permissible for anyone to punish with Allah's punishment.'"""
"1617","Ja'far bin Muhammad narrated from his father that Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said regarding Ibn Muljam when he wounded him: ""Feed him, give him drink, and keep him imprisoned in a good manner. If I survive, I am the guardian of my own blood; if I wish, I will forgive him, and if I wish, I will take retribution. And if I am martyred, then kill him, but do not mutilate him."""
"1618","Ja'far bin Muhammad narrated from his father, who narrated from his grandfather, who said that a book was found attached to the hilt of the sword of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, stating: ""Indeed, among the people, the greatest wrongdoer in the sight of Allah, the Exalted and Glorious, is the killer who kills one who does not fight, and who kills someone other than his own killer. And whoever takes as his guardian anyone other than his own masters has indeed denied the revelation which Allah, the Exalted, sent down upon Muhammad ﷺ."""
"1619","Muhammad bin Ishaq narrated that I asked Abu Ja'far Muhammad bin Ali, ""What was in the scroll that was in the sheath of the Messenger of Allah’s ﷺ sword?"" He replied: ""It contained that Allah has cursed the one who kills someone other than his killer, and has also cursed the one who strikes someone other than his striker. And whoever gives someone’s blessing to a non-guardian as an owner, he has denied the revelation that Allah Almighty sent down upon Muhammad ﷺ."""
"1620","It is narrated from Amr bin Aws, he said: Previously, a person would be seized because of another's sin, until Ibrahim (peace be upon him) came, and Allah Almighty said: ""And it was in the scriptures of Ibrahim that no person will bear the burden of another."" (__QUR_N__: An-Najm: 37, 38)"
"1621","It is narrated from Abu Rimtha (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: ""I went with my father to the presence of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), and my father saw something on the back of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said: 'Allow me to treat what is on your back, for I am a physician.' The Prophet (ﷺ) said: 'You are a good companion.' And the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) asked: 'Who is this with you?' He replied: 'This is my son, I bear witness to him.' The Prophet (ﷺ) said: 'Beware! You will not be held accountable for your son's faults, nor will your son be held accountable for your faults.'"""
"1622","It is narrated from Abdur Rahman bin Bilmani that a man from among the Muslims killed a man from among the Dhimmis. When this matter was presented before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, he ﷺ said: ""I am the most entitled to fulfill my covenant."" Then he ﷺ gave the order regarding him, and he (the Muslim) was killed (in retribution)."
"1623","Abu al-Junub al-Asadi narrated that a man from among the Muslims was brought to Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) who had killed a man from among the Dhimmis. When the testimony was established against him, Ali ordered his execution. Then the brother of the slain man came and said: ""I have forgiven him."" Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""Perhaps they have frightened or troubled you?"" He replied: ""No, but killing him will not bring my brother back. They have given me the blood money and I am satisfied."" Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""You know best. Yes, the blood of one whose protection is our responsibility is like our blood, and his blood money is like our blood money."""
"1624","It is narrated from Mujahid and Hasan (may Allah have mercy on them) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said on the day of the conquest of Makkah: ""A believer will not be killed in retaliation for a disbeliever."""
"1625","It is narrated from Abu Juhaifah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: I asked Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), ""Do you have anything from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ apart from the Qur'an?"" He replied: ""By Him who split the grain and created the soul, we have nothing except the understanding that Allah gives to a servant in His Book, and what is in this scroll."" I asked, ""What is in this scroll?"" He said: ""The rulings of blood money, the rulings of freeing captives, and that no Muslim will be killed in retaliation for a disbeliever."" In another place it is mentioned: ""No believer will be killed in retaliation for a disbeliever."""
"1626","Abu Juhaifah (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated that I asked Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), ""Do you have anything from the teachings of the Prophet ﷺ besides the Qur'an?"" He replied, ""By Him who split the grain and created the soul, there is nothing except the understanding which a man is given of the Qur'an, and what is in this scroll."" I asked, ""What is in the scroll?"" He said, ""The rulings of blood money, the commands regarding the freeing of captives, and that no believer should be killed in retaliation for a disbeliever."""
"1627","It is narrated from Ata, Tawus, Mujahid, and Hasan (may Allah have mercy on them) that the Prophet ﷺ said in his sermon in the year of the conquest of Makkah: ""A Muslim will not be killed in retaliation for a disbeliever."" It was asked whether this narration is Mursal, so I said: Yes."
"1628","It is narrated from Zuhri that the son of Shas Jazami killed a man from among the Nabateans of Syria. When this matter was brought before Uthman bin Affan (may Allah be pleased with him), he ordered the killer to be killed. Then Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) and other companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) spoke with Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) and prevented him from carrying out the killing. He then set the blood money at one thousand dinars."
"1629","It is narrated from Saeed bin Musayyib, may Allah have mercy on him, that he said: ""The blood money of every Mu'ahid during their covenant was one thousand dinars."""
"1630","It is narrated from Abu Shurayh Ka'bi (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If someone’s relative is killed, then his heirs have two options. If they wish, they may take blood money, and if they wish, they may take retribution (qisas)."""
"1631","Through another chain of narration, a similar or equivalent narration to the previous hadith is also reported from Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (ﷺ)."
"1632","It is narrated from Abu Shurayh Ka’bi (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said in the year of the conquest of Makkah: “Whoever has a relative killed, he has two options: if he wishes, he may take blood money, and if he wishes, then retribution (qisas) is for him.” Abu Hanifah said: I said to Ibn Abi Dhi’b: O Abu al-Harith! Will you accept this hadith? (i.e., will you act upon it?) Ibn Abi Dhi’b struck my chest, raised his voice at me, insulted me, and said: I narrate to you the hadith of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and you say, ‘Will you accept it?’ Yes! I will accept it, and it is obligatory upon me and upon everyone who hears this hadith. Indeed, Allah Almighty chose Muhammad (ﷺ) from among the people and guided people through him, and He chose for the people the same religion that He chose for him (ﷺ). Therefore, it is obligatory upon the creation to follow him (ﷺ) in every circumstance, for a Muslim has no other option. Abu Hanifah said: He did not stop saying these things to me until I wished he would become silent."
"1633","It is narrated from Abu Shurayh Ka‘bi (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: “Indeed, Allah has made Makkah a sacred city; it was not made sacred by the people. It is not permissible for anyone who believes in Allah and the Last Day to shed blood therein, nor to cut down any of its trees. And if anyone seeks a concession for himself, then say (to him): This was made lawful for the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), because Allah made it lawful for me, and not for the people, and even for me it was made lawful only for a short part of the day. Then it returned to being sacred as it was yesterday. O people of Khuza‘ah! Surely you have killed a man from the tribe of Hudhayl, and by Allah, I will pay his blood money. And whoever kills someone after this, his heirs have two options: if they wish, they may kill (in retaliation), and if they wish, they may accept blood money.”"
"1634","Muqatil narrated that I took this interpretation from a group of memorizers, among whom were Mu’adh, Mujahid, Hasan, and Dahhak bin Muzahim. Regarding Allah Almighty’s statement, “Whoever is pardoned by his brother,” (al-Baqarah: 178), it is said that for the people of the Torah, retribution (qisas) was obligatory for anyone who killed unjustly; they were neither permitted to pardon nor to accept blood money (diyah). For the people of the Gospel, pardoning was obligatory; they could not kill in retribution. And for the Ummah of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), a concession was given: if they wish, they may kill (in retribution), if they wish, they may accept blood money, and if they wish, they may pardon. And this is the meaning of Allah’s statement: “This is a concession and mercy from your Lord.” They say that blood money is a concession from Allah Almighty; when blood money is accepted, then killing will not take place. Then He said: “And whoever transgresses after that, for him is a painful punishment.” And regarding Allah’s statement: “In retribution there is life for you,” it is said that because of the fear of being killed in retribution, you refrain from killing one another."
"1635","Mujahid says: I heard Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) saying that retribution (qisas) was obligatory upon the Children of Israel and there was no blood money (diyah) among them. So Allah Almighty prescribed this ruling for this Ummah: ""Retribution for the slain has been made obligatory upon you: the free for the free, the slave for the slave, the woman for the woman. But if any remission is made to one by his brother, then let there be a suitable follow-up and payment to him with good conduct. This is a concession and mercy from your Lord."" This is in contrast to what was made obligatory upon those before you. ""But whoever transgresses after that will have a painful punishment."" (__QUR_N__ al-Baqarah: 178)"
"1636","Abu Laila narrated that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Whoever kills a believer unjustly has purchased retribution with his own hands, unless the heirs of the slain are pleased (to forgive). And whoever intervenes in this matter, upon him is the curse of Allah and His wrath; Allah will not accept from him any voluntary or obligatory acts."""
"1637","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Beware! Indeed, for a person killed by intentional mistake (who dies from a whip or a stick), there are one hundred large camels (as blood money). Among them, forty are pregnant camels with young in their wombs."""
"1638","It is narrated from Uqbah bin Aws, may Allah have mercy on him, that it is also narrated from a companion of the Prophet ﷺ in a manner similar to the previous hadith."
"1639","It is narrated from Tawus (may Allah have mercy on him) that he narrated from the Prophet ﷺ that he ﷺ said: ""Whoever is killed in a riot, whoever among the fighters is killed by a stone, or by a whip, or by a blow from a stick, then that is accidental killing; its blood money is the blood money for accidental killing. And whoever is killed intentionally, then (the killer) has purchased retribution with his own hands. And whoever intervenes in this, upon him is the curse of Allah and His wrath; neither voluntary worship nor obligatory worship will be accepted from him."""
"1640","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) said: ""Beware! Indeed, in the case of a person killed by mistake resembling intentional murder, which is done with a whip or a stick, the compensation is one hundred camels, of which forty are pregnant she-camels with offspring in their wombs."""
"1641","Urwah (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated that Abu Hudhaifah bin Yaman (may Allah be pleased with him) was an old man. On the day of the Battle of Uhud, he was kept with the women at a high place. From there, he came out seeking martyrdom. Then, coming from the direction of the polytheists, the Muslims quickly surrounded him and struck him with their swords, while his son Hudhaifah (may Allah be pleased with him) was saying to the Companions: ""This is my father, this is my father!"" Due to the heat of battle, they did not listen to him until they killed him. Then Hudhaifah (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""May Allah forgive you, and He is the Most Merciful of those who show mercy."" Then the Prophet (ﷺ) ordered the payment of his blood money."
"1642","It is narrated from Qais bin Abi Hazim, he said: A people sought refuge with the tribe of Jashm. Then, when the Muslims overpowered them, they sought protection through prostration, but the Muslims killed some of them. When this matter reached the Prophet ﷺ, he said: ""Because of their prayers, give them half the blood money."" Then on this occasion he said: ""Beware! I am free from every such Muslim who stays among the polytheists."" The Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) asked: ""O Messenger of Allah ﷺ! What is the reason for this?"" He ﷺ said: ""Their fires should not be visible together."""
"1643","Abdullah bin Abu Bakr narrated from his father that the letter which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote to Amr bin Hazm (may Allah be pleased with him), in it is stated: ""One hundred camels are for (the killing of) one soul."""
"1644","It is narrated from Abdullah bin Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding the book of blood money that was sent from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) to Amr bin Hazm (may Allah be pleased with him), that it states: ""For a life, there are one hundred camels."" Ibn Jurayj said: I asked Abdullah bin Abu Bakr: ""Do you have any doubt that it is from the Book of Allah?"" He replied: ""No."""
"1645","It is also narrated in a similar manner through another chain from Tawus (may Allah have mercy on him)."
"1646","It is narrated from Amr bin Shu'aib (may Allah have mercy on him) that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to fix the price of camels for the people of the town at four hundred dinars or its equivalent in silver (dirhams), which would be divided according to the price of camels. When camels became expensive, he would increase its price, and when they became cheaper, he would decrease its price. The people of the town are obliged to pay the price that is current at that time."
"1647","It is narrated from Mak’hool and Ata’ (may Allah have mercy on them), they said: “We found people saying that the blood money (diyah) of a free Muslim during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was one hundred camels. Then Umar ibn al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) set the diyah for townspeople at one thousand dinars or twelve thousand dirhams. And for a free Muslim woman among the townspeople, the diyah was five hundred dinars or six thousand dirhams. If the killer was a Bedouin, then her diyah was fifty camels, and the diyah for a Bedouin woman, if killed by a Bedouin, was also set at fifty camels. And he said: ‘A Bedouin should not be made responsible for payment in gold or silver.’”"
"1648","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (ﷺ) gave the ruling, regarding the child of a woman from Banu Lihyan who was born dead due to being struck by another woman, that as blood money a slave man or slave woman should be given. Then he said that the woman who caused the miscarriage, about whom the Prophet (ﷺ) had given the verdict, passed away, so the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ruled that her inheritance is for her sons and husband, and the payment of the blood money is upon her 'asaba (male relatives on the father's side)."
"1649","Imam Shafi’i, may Allah have mercy on him, said: If someone asks, “How is it regarding the matter in which the Prophet ﷺ gave the ruling of paying blood money for the fetus to the woman?” then it will be said: A trustworthy person has informed us. Al-Rabi’ said: He is Yahya bin Hassan. He narrated from Al-Layth bin Sa’d, who narrated from Ibn Shihab, who narrated from Ibn al-Musayyib, who narrated from Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him."
"1650","It is narrated from Ibn Musayyib (may Allah have mercy on him) that the Prophet ﷺ gave the verdict of giving a slave or a slave-girl as compensation for the child who is killed in the womb of his mother. The one against whom the verdict was given said: ""How can I pay compensation for something that has neither drunk nor eaten, neither spoken nor made any sound at the time of birth? In such a case, would the compensation not be wasted?"" Upon this, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""This person seems to be a brother of the soothsayers."""
"1651","It is narrated from Tawoos (may Allah have mercy on him) that Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) asked: ""I put under oath by Allah the one who has heard anything from the Prophet ﷺ regarding the fetus (unborn child in the womb)?"" So Haml bin Malik bin Nabighah (may Allah be pleased with him) stood up and said: ""I used to live between my two wives. One of them struck the other with a tent pole, and she miscarried a dead fetus. In this matter, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled for a slave or a slave-girl."" Then Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""It was close that we would have given a verdict in this matter based on our own opinion."""
"1652","It is narrated from Tawus that Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""Is there anyone who has heard anything from the Prophet ﷺ regarding the fetus?"" Then Haml bin Malik bin Nabighah (may Allah be pleased with him) stood up and said: ""I was living with my two co-wives when one of them struck the other with a tent pole, causing her to miscarry a dead child. In this matter, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled for a slave or a slave-girl."" Then Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""If we had not heard this, we would have given a different verdict in this case."""
"1653","It is narrated from Ibn Musayyib (may Allah have mercy on him), he said: ""The blood money (diyah) of a slave is in his price."""
"1654","It is narrated from Sa'id bin al-Musayyib, may Allah have mercy on him, that he said: ""The blood money (diyah) of a slave is in his value, just as the wound of a free man is in his blood money (diyah)."""
"1655","It is narrated from Sadaqah bin Yasar, may Allah have mercy on him, who said: We sent a message to Sa'id bin al-Musayyib, may Allah have mercy on him, asking him about the blood money (diyah) of a contractee (dhimmi). He replied that Uthman bin Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, had decided it to be four thousand (dirhams). Sadaqah says: We asked, ""Who killed him?"" He said, then he threw pebbles at us. Imam Shafi'i, may Allah have mercy on him, said: These were the people who asked him this question at the end."
"1656","It is narrated from Sadaqah bin Yasar: We sent a message to Sa'id bin al-Musayyib (may Allah have mercy on him) and asked about the blood money (diyah) of a Jew and a Christian. Sa'id (may Allah have mercy on him) replied: ""Uthman bin Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) decided that four thousand should be paid in this case."""
"1657","It is narrated from Saeed bin Musayyib (may Allah have mercy on him), who narrates from Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him), that he gave a ruling of four thousand (dirhams) for a Jew and a Christian, and eight hundred (dirhams) for a Magian."
"1658","Abdullah bin Abu Bakr narrated from his father that in the book which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote for Amr bin Hazm (may Allah be pleased with him), it is stated: ""When the entire nose is cut off, its compensation is one hundred camels. For a head wound, the compensation is one third of the blood money; for a wound in the abdomen or similar, also one third; for a wound in the eye, fifty; for the hand, fifty; and for the foot, fifty camels. For each finger, ten camels; for a tooth, five; and for a wound that exposes the bone, the compensation is also five camels."""
"1659","It is narrated from Muhammad bin Amr bin Hazm that in the book which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote for Amr bin Hazm (may Allah be pleased with him), it is stated: ""For each finger, (the blood money is) ten camels."""
"1660","Abu Musa Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""There are ten (camels) in the fingers."""
"1661","It is narrated from Sa'id bin al-Musayyib (may Allah have mercy on him) that 'Umar bin al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) ruled that for the thumb, the compensation is fifteen (camels), for the finger next to the thumb (the index finger), ten, for the middle finger, ten, for the finger next to the little finger, nine, and for the little finger, six (camels as blood money)."
"1662","It is narrated from Aslam (may Allah be pleased with him), the freed slave of Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him), that Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) gave the verdict of one camel (as blood money) for a molar tooth, one camel for a collarbone, and one camel for a rib."
"1663","Abu Ghatfan bin Tarif Muzani narrated that Marwan bin Hakam sent him to Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) to ask about the blood money for a molar tooth. Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) replied: ""It is five camels."" (The narrator says) Marwan sent me again to Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) and said: ""Do you consider the front part of the mouth like the molars?"" Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) replied: ""Even if you do not accept it, the blood money for all the fingers is equal."" Imam Shafi'i (may Allah have mercy on him) said: ""This hadith indicates that the blood money for both lips is also equal. And there are other reports from the companions (may Allah be pleased with them) regarding the blood money for the lips."""
"1664","Abdullah bin Abu Bakr narrated from his father that in the book which the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wrote for Amr bin Hazm (may Allah be pleased with him), it is stated: ""For a wound that exposes the bone (mudihah), there are five camels."""
"1665","It is narrated from Saeed bin Musayyib (may Allah have mercy on him) that Umar and Uthman (may Allah be pleased with them both) gave the verdict of half the blood money (diyah) for a ""multa’ah"" (the membrane between the skull bone and flesh being cut) as is given for a ""mudiha"" (a wound that exposes the bone)."
"1666","It is also narrated through another chain from Ibn Musayyib that a narration similar to the previous hadith is reported from Umar and Uthman (may Allah be pleased with them both)."
"1667","Imam Shafi’i (may Allah have mercy on him) said: “Whoever heard from Ibn Nafi’, he informed me that he narrates from Imam Malik (may Allah have mercy on him) with the same chain regarding a narration similar to this (previous hadith).” Imam Shafi’i (may Allah have mercy on him) said: “And we read before Imam Malik (may Allah have mercy on him) that we do not know anyone among the predecessors or the current Imams who has given any ruling (of blood money) for any wound less than a ‘muwaddiha’ (a wound exposing the bone).”"
"1668","It is narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""The wound caused by an animal is pardoned."""
